{
  "_": [
    "SHARED ARTIFACT. This file is byte-identical in writeitgreat-llc/website",
    "(ci/analytics_channel_fixture.json) and writeitgreat-llc/proposal-evaluation",
    "(ci/analytics_channel_fixture.json), and it pins the rules module that is",
    "likewise byte-identical in both: website app/analytics_channel_rules.py,",
    "proposal-evaluation analytics_channel_rules.py.",
    "",
    "TO CHANGE THE RULES: edit the rules module, bump its RULES_VERSION, copy the",
    "WHOLE module and this WHOLE file to the other repo, paste the new digest into",
    "rules_sha256 in both, and add a vector proving what you changed. Run",
    "`python ci/check_channel_parity.py` in each repo; it prints the digest it",
    "computed when it does not match.",
    "",
    "WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT GUARANTEE: the two repos are separate, one public",
    "and one private, with no shared package and no network access from CI. So NO",
    "check here can make repo B go red because repo A changed. What it does buy:",
    "touching the rules in either repo turns THAT repo red until the shared files",
    "and the digest are updated together, which is the moment to port. The only",
    "cross-repo detector with real teeth is the runtime one: both collectors report",
    "rules_version on the analytics ingest envelope, so the dashboard sees the two",
    "sites disagreeing within minutes of a one-sided deploy.",
    "",
    "channels[] is the vocabulary both classifiers emit. wig-dashboard's",
    "WA_CHANNELS is this set PLUS 'unknown', which is the receiver's bucket for an",
    "event that arrived with no channel — so the right relationship there is",
    "subset, not equality. Do not 'fix' either side to match the other."
  ],
